From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Steinhauf <daniel@steinhauf.eu>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 01:18:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: rtl8365mb: add hardware LAG / trunk offload

Add DSA port_lag_join/leave/change hooks and program the RTL8367-class
trunk tables so two user ports can hash in hardware when enslaved to a
Linux bond.

- set ds->num_lag_ids so DSA assigns lag->id (required for port_lag_join)
- allow single-member join in lag_can_offload (program HW at 2 members)
- limit trunk groups to 0-1; they share the hash map at 0x08d2/0x08d3.
  Leave that map at the chip default; it is the user-defined map and
  the trunk runs in dumb mode.
- hash on the ingress port (SPA) as well, so two nodes whose addresses
  share an SMAC/SIP bucket do not land on the same member
- leave trunk flood off; it pins unknown unicast to the first member
- enable trunk dumb mode (CPU LACP + ASIC data plane)
- trap LACP RMA 01:80:c2:00:00:02 to CPU (RMA_CTRL02); HW trunk
  otherwise swallows partner LACPDUs so bonding never sees RX

DSA calls the LAG ops under rtnl, which serializes the trunk state in
realtek_priv, so the driver takes no lock of its own.

The PORT_TRUNK_* register map and dumb-mode semantics follow the Realtek
rtl8367c vendor SDK; validated on the RTL8370MB-CG of a Turing Pi 2.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Steinhauf <daniel@steinhauf.eu>
